pt-PT.ranks.txt.gz is made from FrequencyWords by Hermit Dave
(https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords), its European Portuguese list
of the 50,000 most common words, content/2018/pt/pt_50k.txt, at commit
525f9b560de45753a5ea01069454e72e9aa541c6. FrequencyWords is built from the
OpenSubtitles 2018 corpus of OPUS
(https://opus.nlpl.eu/legacy/OpenSubtitles-v2018.php), with subtitles from
http://www.opensubtitles.org/:

  P. Lison and J. Tiedemann, 2016, OpenSubtitles2016: Extracting Large
  Parallel Corpora from Movie and TV Subtitles. In Proceedings of the 10th
  International Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation (LREC 2016).
  https://aclanthology.org/L16-1147/

FrequencyWords' content is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0), as its
README says ("CC-by-sa-4.0 for content").

Modified: filtered to the words of the Portuguese (Portugal) dictionary
(pt-PT.txt.gz) and converted to ranks, most common first, one a line. A word
spelt as before the 1990 spelling reform ("acção", "óptimo") has its count
added to its new spelling ("ação", "ótimo"), when only the new one is in the
dictionary. The program that does this is frequencywords/main.go, beside
this file.

